 mapping and genome-wide association studies</article-title><source>Nat Rev Genet</source><year>2009</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>285</fpage><lpage>290</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nrg2571</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19337289</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ahmad-Nejad</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>H&#x000e4;cker</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Rutz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bauer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Vabulas</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bacterial CpG-DNA and lipopolysaccharides activate Toll-like receptors at distinct cellular compartments</article-title><source>Eur J Immunol</source><year>2002</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>1958</fpage><lpage>1968</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/1521-4141(200207)32:7&#x0003c;1958::AID-IMMU1958&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-U</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12115616</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaisho</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Akira</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Toll-like receptors and their signaling mechanism in innate immunity</article-title><source>Acta Odontol Scand</source><year>2001</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>124</fpage><lpage>130</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/000163501750266701</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11501880</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hemmi</surname><given-names>